# Agent Guide for `{{ repo_name }}`

This file is for AI coding agents working in this repository. It states how
to run the checks and where edits belong. The human-facing contribution
guide is [.github/CONTRIBUTING.md](.github/CONTRIBUTING.md).
{% if kaggle %}
> Kaggle competition project: shared helpers live in `src/utils/`
> (`from utils.config import ...`); competition data goes in `src/input/`
> and predictions are written to `src/output/`. Do not commit data,
> predictions, or logs — they are git-ignored.
{% elif oj_code %}
> Code-submission workspace ({{ oj_kind }}): write solutions as single files
> (e.g. `main.py`). Per-problem folders and `test/` sample cases are created
> by the judge CLI at runtime — do not commit downloaded cases.
{% elif oj_ctf %}
> CTF participant workspace: per-problem starters live in
> `challenges/<category>/<problem>/solve.py`. Run one directly
> (`python challenges/pwn/example/solve.py`), then adapt the offset /
> target. Never commit binaries (`vuln`) or flags — they are git-ignored.
{% elif web_api %}
> Web API service: the application lives in the top-level `app/` package
> (no `<pkg>` library). Run it with `uvicorn app.main:app --reload`.
{% if data_science_layout %}
>
> The data-science layer coexists: `src/` holds the analysis pipeline
> (`data/`, `features/`, `models/`, `visualization/`) and `notebooks/` /
> `reports/` the exploration artifacts. Keep heavy analysis out of `app/`;
> routers expose results computed by `src/` code. Do not commit data,
> models or reports — they are git-ignored.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
## Commands

The `{{ task_runner_effective }}` task runner drives the common commands:

```sh
{% if task_runner_effective == 'task' %}task fix            # auto-fix formatting and lint
task lint           # ruff format --check + ruff check (check-only)
task test           # pytest{% if strictness in ['recommended', 'full'] %}
task type-check     # type checker + static analysis{% endif %}
task check          # everything above
{% elif task_runner_effective == 'just' %}just fix            # auto-fix formatting and lint
just lint
just test
just check
{% elif task_runner_effective == 'make' %}make fix
make lint
make test
make check
{% elif task_runner_effective == 'poe' %}poe fix
poe lint
poe test
poe check
{% elif task_runner_effective == 'invoke' %}invoke fix
invoke lint
invoke test
invoke check
{% elif task_runner_effective == 'duty' %}duty fix
duty lint
duty test
duty check
{% else %}pixi run -e dev fix
pixi run -e dev lint
pixi run -e dev test
pixi run -e dev check
{% endif %}```

Run `{{ task_runner_effective }} fix` before committing to apply formatting
and lint fixes, then `{{ task_runner_effective }} check` (or `lint` + `test`
{% if strictness in ['recommended', 'full'] %}+ `type-check` {% endif %}individually) before finishing a change.
The repo-hygiene checks (secrets, workflow linting, YAML validity,
conventional commit messages) run in CI, not as local hooks — the lint and
fix tasks work anywhere, including outside a git repository.
{% if strictness in ['recommended', 'full'] %}
Type checking uses basedpyright plus `{{ type_checker }}`; `deptry`,
`vulture`, and `typos` also run as part of type-check.
{% else %}
Type checking is minimal at `strictness: {{ strictness }}` — pytest and
ruff are the checks that matter.
{% endif %}
{% if docs %}
Build the docs with `{{ task_runner_effective }} docs`.
{% endif %}
## Where to edit

- Application/package code: `{{ pkg_dir }}/`
- Tests: `tests/`
- Docs: `README.md`{% if docs %} and `docs/`{% endif %}

Keep 100% coverage where it exists; do not lower it.
{% if scraping_effective %}
## Web-fetching rules (Good-future charter)

- Every web fetch goes through `{{ pkg_dir }}/fetcher.py`
{% if scraping_scrapy_effective %}  (or the `{{ pkg_dir }}/spider.py` spider)
{% endif %}{% if scraping_memorious_effective %}  (or the `{{ pkg_dir }}/crawler.py` crawler)
{% endif %}{% if scraping_playwright_effective %}  (or `{{ pkg_dir }}/browser_fetch.py` for JS-rendered pages)
{% endif %}  — never call `requests.get` / `httpx.get` / `urlopen` directly
  (ruff `banned-api` fails the build).
- Read [CHARTER.md](CHARTER.md) before touching fetch code: robots.txt,
  1 req/s per host, disk cache, contactable User-Agent.
- Never generate CAPTCHA-solving helpers. If a site blocks bots, stop and
  ask the maintainer — do not bypass the protection.
{% endif %}
{% if data_science_layout %}
Data, notebooks, and reports (`data/`, `notebooks/`, `models/`,
`reports/`) are analysis artifacts — keep generated outputs out of git.
{% endif %}
## Commits and CI

- Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/)
  (`feat:`, `fix:`, ...); the commit-msg hook enforces it.
- CI runs lint, type-check, and tests on every push
{% if docs %} plus a docs build{% endif %}; keep all of them green.
